abstract: >
  ANNE (Adaptive Neural Nexus Engine) is a six-stage cognitive architecture
  designed for semantic validation during inference, ethical decision-making,
  fractal memory, and runtime learning. It combines a Mythos curiosity engine
  with a structured ethical core (Human-First ADS) to address hallucination
  and alignment challenges in current LLM systems.
keywords:
  - cognitive architecture
  - ethical AI
  - hallucination reduction
  - fractal memory
  - multi-agent systems
  - human-aligned AI
